.SH "NAME"
pcre2_maketables_free \- free character tables
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\fB\&#include\fP \fB<pcre2.h>\fP

\fBvoid\fP pcre2_maketables_free(\fBpcre2_general_context\fP *\fIgcontext\fP,
                           \fBconst\fP \fBuint8_t\fP *\fItables\fP);
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function discards a set of character tables that were created by a call
to
pcre2_maketables().
.sp
The \fIgcontext\fP parameter should match what was used in that call to
account for any custom allocators that might be in use; if it is \f(CRNULL\fP
the system \f(CRfree()\fP is used.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page.